"Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit\n"
"Plural-Forms: nplurals=3; plural=(n%10==1 && n%100!=11 ? 0 : n%10>=2 && "
"n%10<=4 && (n%100<10 || n%100>=20) ? 1 : 2);\n"

#. Translators: The title of the window that lists the fragments of a checklist
#. item so that one of them can be copied to the clipboard.
msgid "Copy a fragment"
msgstr "Копіювати фрагмент"

#. Translators: The label of the list of the fragments of a checklist item, one
#. of which is about to be copied to the clipboard.
msgid "Fragments"
msgstr "Фрагменти"

#. Translators: The label of the button that puts the selected fragment of the
#. checklist item in the clipboard. Enter on the list does the same.
msgid "Copy"
msgstr "Копіювати"

#. Translators: The label of the button that closes the list of fragments without
#. copying anything. Escape does the same.
#. Translators: The label of the button of the item dialog that closes it without
#. writing anything. Escape does the same.
msgid "Cancel"
msgstr "Скасувати"

# The product name is deliberately left in English in every locale: it is the name the
# add-on carries in the Add-on Store, in the configuration directory and in its documentation.
#. Translators: The title of the add-on's own window, which shows the whole
#. checklist. It is the product name, which is not translated in any locale.
#. Translators: The title of the add-on's windows: the product name, which is
#. not translated in any locale.
#. Translators: The name of the category this add-on's commands appear under
#. in NVDA's Input Gestures dialog.
#. Translators: The add-on's entry in the Tools menu of NVDA, which opens the
#. window showing the whole checklist. It is the product name, which is not
#. translated in any locale.
#. Add-on summary/title, usually the user visible name of the add-on
#. Translators: Summary/title for this add-on
#. to be shown on installation and add-on information found in add-on store
msgid "Axygen Checklist"
msgstr "Axygen Checklist"

#. Translators: The label of the tree of the add-on's window, which holds every
#. section of the checklist and every item in them.
msgid "Checklist"
msgstr "Чекліст"

#. Translators: The label of the read-only panel under the tree of the add-on's
#. window, which shows the comment left on the selected checklist item.
#. Translators: The label of the editable field of the item dialog, where the tester
#. writes their conclusion about the checklist item.
msgid "Comment"
msgstr "Коментар"

#. Translators: The title of the window that shows one checklist item in full and
#. is the only place a comment is written.
msgid "Checklist item"
msgstr "Пункт чекліста"

#. Translators: The label of the read-only field of the item dialog holding the
#. whole text of the checklist item.
msgid "Item"
msgstr "Пункт"

#. Translators: The label of the read-only field of the item dialog holding the
#. note the author of the checklist wrote about this item. The field is there
#. only for an item that carries one.
msgid "Note"
msgstr "Нотатка"

#. Translators: The label of the combo box of the item dialog, where the status of
#. the checklist item is chosen.
msgid "Status"
msgstr "Статус"

#. Translators: The label of the button of the item dialog that writes the status
#. and the comment to the checklist file. The letter after the ampersand is the
#. mnemonic that activates it.
msgid "&Save"
msgstr "&Зберегти"

#. Translators: The title of the dialog that picks a checklist file to open.
msgid "Open a checklist"
msgstr "Відкрити чекліст"

#. Translators: The kind of file the Open dialog offers, shown in its file type
#. filter. The pattern "(*.json)" is added after it.
msgid "Checklist files"
msgstr "Файли чеклістів"

#. Translators: The second entry of the Open dialog's file type filter, which
#. shows every file rather than only checklists. The pattern "(*.*)" is added
#. after it.
msgid "All files"
msgstr "Усі файли"

#. Translators: The status of a checklist item that has been checked and works.
msgid "passed"
msgstr "пройдено"

#. Translators: Stands in front of the text of a checklist item in the tree of the
#. add-on's window, when the item has been checked and works. The colon and the space
#. are part of it.
msgid "Passed: "
msgstr "Пройдено: "

#. Translators: The status of a checklist item that has been checked and does not work.
msgid "failed"
msgstr "провалено"

#. Translators: Stands in front of the text of a checklist item in the tree of the
#. add-on's window, when the item has been checked and does not work. The colon and
#. the space are part of it.
msgid "Failed: "
msgstr "Провалено: "

#. Translators: The status of a checklist item that could not be checked because
#. something else is in the way.
msgid "blocked"
msgstr "заблоковано"

#. Translators: Stands in front of the text of a checklist item in the tree of the
#. add-on's window, when the item could not be checked because something else is in
#. the way. The colon and the space are part of it.
msgid "Blocked: "
msgstr "Заблоковано: "

#. Translators: The status of a checklist item that was deliberately left unchecked.
msgid "skipped"
msgstr "пропущено"

#. Translators: Stands in front of the text of a checklist item in the tree of the
#. add-on's window, when the item was deliberately left unchecked. The colon and the
#. space are part of it.
msgid "Skipped: "
msgstr "Пропущено: "

#. Translators: The status of a checklist item that has not been checked yet.
msgid "not checked"
msgstr "не перевірено"

#. Translators: Spoken after the status of a checklist item the tester has
#. commented on. The comment itself is not spoken; the item dialog shows it.
msgid "has a comment"
msgstr "є коментар"

#. Translators: Spoken after a save from the item dialog that left a comment on the
#. item. The status word goes in front of it when that changed too, running straight
#. on: "failed, comment saved".
msgid "comment saved"
msgstr "коментар збережено"

#. Translators: Spoken after a save from the item dialog emptied a comment the item
#. was carrying.
msgid "comment deleted"
msgstr "коментар видалено"

#. Translators: Spoken when a checklist file was written by a newer version of
#. the add-on than the one running, which cannot know what is in it.
msgid "This file was created by a newer version of the add-on"
msgstr "Файл створено новішою версією додатка"

#. Translators: Spoken when a checklist file cannot be read, or holds something
#. that is not a valid checklist.
msgid "Error reading the file"
msgstr "Помилка читання файлу"

#. Translators: Shown above the reason a checklist file was refused, naming where in
#. the file the problem is. {section} counts the sections of the file from one.
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Section {section}"
msgstr "Розділ {section}"

#. Translators: Shown above the reason a checklist file was refused, naming where in the
#. file the problem is. {section} and {item} count the sections of the file, and the items
#. of that section, from one.
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Section {section}, item {item}"
msgstr "Розділ {section}, пункт {item}"

#. Translators: Added to the place a problem in a checklist file was found at, when the
#. item there carries a usable id. {id} is the value of the item's "id" field, which is
#. what the author of the file would search for.
#, python-brace-format
msgid ", id {id}"
msgstr ", id {id}"

#. A file in some other encoding arrives here too: section 2 puts it
#. under the same answer, because which encoding the author had in mind
#. is not something the add-on can say.
#. Translators: Shown when a checklist file the tester picked cannot be parsed.
msgid "The file is not valid JSON."
msgstr "Файл не є коректним JSON."

#. Translators: Shown when a checklist file the tester picked leaves out a field
#. the format requires. {field} is the name of that field, as it is spelled in the
#. file.
#, python-brace-format
msgid "The required field \"{field}\" is missing."
msgstr "Обов'язкове поле «{field}» відсутнє."

#. Translators: Shown when a field of a checklist file the tester picked holds the
#. wrong kind of value. {field} is the name of the field and {value} is what stands
#. there, written the way the file spells it.
#, python-brace-format
msgid "The field \"{field}\" must be text, but holds {value}."
msgstr "Поле «{field}» має бути текстом, а містить {value}."

#. Translators: Shown when a field of a checklist file the tester picked holds the
#. wrong kind of value. {field} is the name of the field and {value} is what stands
#. there, written the way the file spells it.
#, python-brace-format
msgid "The field \"{field}\" must be a whole number, but holds {value}."
msgstr "Поле «{field}» має бути цілим числом, а містить {value}."

#. Translators: Shown when a field of a checklist file the tester picked holds the
#. wrong kind of value. {field} is the name of the field and {value} is what stands
#. there, written the way the file spells it.
#, python-brace-format
msgid "The field \"{field}\" must be a list, but holds {value}."
msgstr "Поле «{field}» має бути списком, а містить {value}."

#. Translators: Shown when a checklist file the tester picked holds no sections at
#. all. Flat checklists without sections are not supported.
msgid ""
"The field \"sections\" is empty; a checklist needs at least one section."
msgstr "Поле «sections» порожнє: чекліст потребує щонайменше одного розділу."

#. Translators: Shown when two items of a checklist file the tester picked carry
#. the same id, which has to be unique within the file. {value} is that id.
#, python-brace-format
msgid "The id {value} belongs to more than one item."
msgstr "Ідентифікатор {value} належить більш ніж одному пункту."

#. Translators: Shown when an item of a checklist file the tester picked carries a
#. status outside the five the format allows. {value} is what stands there, written
#. the way the file spells it.
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The field \"status\" holds {value}, which is not one of \"pending\", "
"\"passed\", \"failed\", \"blocked\" and \"skipped\"."
msgstr ""
"Поле «status» містить {value} — значення, якого немає серед «pending», "
"«passed», «failed», «blocked» і «skipped»."

#. Translators: Shown when a checklist file the tester picked declares a format
#. version this add-on does not know and which is not a later one either, so there
#. is no update to send anyone to. {value} is the version the file declares.
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The field \"format_version\" holds {value}, which is not a version of this "
"format."
msgstr "Поле «format_version» містить {value} — це не версія цього формату."

#. Translators: Shown when a checklist file the tester picked does not hold a JSON
#. object at its top level, so there is no checklist in it at all.
msgid "The file does not hold a checklist."
msgstr "Файл не містить чекліста."

#. Translators: Shown when an entry of the "sections" list of a checklist file is not
#. a section at all, but a number, a piece of text or a list.
msgid "This section is not written as a section."
msgstr "Цей розділ записано не як розділ."

#. Translators: Shown when an entry of the "items" list of a checklist file is not an item
#. at all, but a number, a piece of text or a list.
msgid "This item is not written as an item."
msgstr "Цей пункт записано не як пункт."

#. Translators: Spoken when a change to the checklist could not be written to the
#. file, so it is in memory but not on disk.
msgid "Error writing the file"
msgstr "Помилка запису файлу"

# The first form covers 1, 21, 31 and so on, where "всі" reads as a flourish in
# Ukrainian too; the other two carry it.
#. Translators: Spoken when the last item of a checklist has been given a
#. status, so nothing in it is left unchecked. {count} is how many items
#. the checklist holds. The word "All" is dropped from the singular, where
#. it reads as a flourish over a count of one.
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Checklist complete! {count} item processed"
msgid_plural "Checklist complete! All {count} items processed"
msgstr[0] "Чекліст завершено! Опрацьовано {count} пункт"
msgstr[1] "Чекліст завершено! Опрацьовано всі {count} пункти"
msgstr[2] "Чекліст завершено! Опрацьовано всі {count} пунктів"

#. Translators: Spoken for the current section of the checklist: its name, how many
#. of its items carry a verdict, and how many it holds in all.
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Section: {name}, {processed} of {total} processed"
msgstr "Розділ: {name}, опрацьовано {processed} з {total}"

#. Translators: Added after a count of checklist items when some of them failed,
#. running straight on from it: "All 12 items processed, 2 failed".
#, python-brace-format
msgid ", {count} failed"
msgstr ", провалено {count}"

#. Translators: Spoken when NVDA starts and the checklist that was open
#. last time is no longer where it was.
msgid "Checklist file not found"
msgstr "Файл чекліста не знайдено"

#. Translators: The description of a command, as it appears in NVDA's Input Gestures dialog.
msgid ""
"Moves to the next item of the checklist. Twice: to the first item of the "
"next section"
msgstr ""
"Переходить до наступного пункту чекліста. Двічі — до першого пункту "
"наступного розділу"

#. Translators: The description of a command, as it appears in NVDA's Input Gestures dialog.
msgid ""
"Moves to the previous item of the checklist. Twice: to the first item of the "
"previous section"
msgstr ""
"Переходить до попереднього пункту чекліста. Двічі — до першого пункту "
"попереднього розділу"

#. Translators: The description of a command, as it appears in NVDA's Input Gestures dialog.
msgid ""
"Marks the current checklist item as passed, or as not checked if it passed "
"already"
msgstr ""
"Позначає поточний пункт чекліста пройденим, а вже пройдений повертає в «не "
"перевірено»"

#. Translators: The description of a command, as it appears in NVDA's Input Gestures dialog.
msgid ""
"Reads the current item of the checklist again. Twice: opens the item dialog"
msgstr ""
"Повторює озвучення поточного пункту чекліста. Двічі — відкриває діалог пункту"

#. Translators: The description of a command, as it appears in NVDA's Input Gestures dialog.
msgid "Arms the command mode of the checklist for three seconds"
msgstr "Озброює режим команд чекліста на три секунди"

#. Translators: The description of a command, as it appears in NVDA's Input Gestures dialog.
msgid "Opens a checklist file"
msgstr "Відкриває файл чекліста"

#. Translators: The description of a command, as it appears in NVDA's Input Gestures dialog.
msgid ""
"Reads the name of the current section of the checklist and the progress "
"through it"
msgstr "Озвучує назву поточного розділу чекліста та прогрес у ньому"

#. Translators: The description of a command, as it appears in NVDA's Input Gestures dialog.
msgid ""
"Resets the current section of the checklist, erasing its statuses and "
"comments"
msgstr "Скидає поточний розділ чекліста, стираючи його статуси й коментарі"

#. Translators: The question asked before the current section of the checklist
#. is reset, that is every item put back to not checked and every comment erased.
msgid ""
"Reset the section? Every status and comment in the section will be erased. "
"This cannot be undone."
msgstr ""
"Скинути розділ? Будуть стерті всі статуси та коментарі розділу. Цю дію не "
"можна відмінити."

#. Translators: The description of a command, as it appears in NVDA's Input Gestures dialog.
msgid "Copies a fragment of the current checklist item to the clipboard"
msgstr "Копіює фрагмент поточного пункту чекліста в буфер обміну"

#. Translators: Spoken when the copy command is used on a checklist item whose
#. text and note hold no fragments to copy.
msgid "The item has no fragments"
msgstr "У пункті немає фрагментів"

#. Translators: The description of a command, as it appears in NVDA's Input Gestures dialog.
msgid ""
"Turns on or off moving to the next checklist item once this one has a verdict"
msgstr ""
"Вмикає або вимикає перехід до наступного пункту чекліста після присвоєння "
"вердикту"

#. Translators: Spoken when auto-advance has just been turned on, so that giving an
#. item a verdict moves on to the next item of the checklist.
msgid "Auto-advance on"
msgstr "Автоперехід увімкнено"

#. Translators: Spoken when auto-advance has just been turned off, so that giving an item
#. a verdict leaves the position on the item it was given to.
msgid "Auto-advance off"
msgstr "Автоперехід вимкнено"

#. Translators: The description of a command, as it appears in NVDA's Input Gestures dialog.
msgid "Opens the window showing the whole checklist"
msgstr "Відкриває вікно, яке показує весь чекліст"

#. Translators: Spoken when there is no section after this one to jump to.
msgid "End of list"
msgstr "Кінець списку"

#. Translators: Spoken when there is no section before this one to jump to.
msgid "Start of list"
msgstr "Початок списку"

#. Translators: Spoken after the current section of the checklist has been reset.
msgid "Section reset"
msgstr "Розділ скинуто"

#. Translators: Spoken when a command is used before a checklist has been opened.
msgid "No checklist loaded"
msgstr "Чекліст не завантажено"

#. Translators: Spoken when a command is used on a checklist whose sections
#. are all empty, so there is no item to stand on.
msgid "The checklist has no items"
msgstr "У чеклісті немає пунктів"

#. Add-on description
#. Translators: Long description to be shown for this add-on on add-on information from add-on store
msgid ""
"Walk a test checklist with global commands while the system focus stays in "
"the application under test.\n"
"Items are marked passed, failed or skipped, commented and read back by "
"speech, without ever leaving the window being tested.\n"
"Checklists are plain JSON files that record the result of the run."
msgstr ""
"Проходить чекліст тестування глобальними командами, лишаючи системний фокус "
"у тестованому застосунку.\n"
"Пункти позначаються як пройдені, провалені чи пропущені, коментуються та "
"озвучуються — не полишаючи вікна, яке перевіряють.\n"
"Чеклісти є звичайними файлами JSON, що зберігають результат прогону."

#. Brief changelog for this version
#. Translators: what's new content for the add-on version to be shown in the add-on store
msgid "First development version."
msgstr "Перша версія в розробці."
